course: dictionary
lesson: 14556
title: Phonetic: words that show sound
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Phonetic is an adjective about sound. Something phonetic is connected with the sounds of speech, the way we say words out loud.
explain: A phonetic spelling writes a word the way it sounds, not the way it is usually spelt. «Fone» is a phonetic spelling of phone, because it shows the sound, not the correct spelling.
explain: Dictionaries use phonetic symbols to show how to say a word. Pilots, police and soldiers also use a phonetic alphabet, such as Alpha, Bravo and Charlie, so that letters are not misheard on the radio.
fact: Phonetic means connected with the sounds of speech.
fact: «Fone» is a phonetic spelling of «phone»: it shows the sound, not the correct spelling.
fact: Dictionaries use phonetic symbols to show how a word is pronounced.
fact: The phonetic alphabet is a set of code words, such as Alpha, Bravo and Charlie, used so that letters are not misheard.
exercise: Which word is a phonetic spelling of «phone»? | phone | *fone | photo
exercise: What does phonetic mean? | Very quiet and gentle | Good at drawing maps | *Connected with the sounds of speech | Written in gold ink
exercise: On the radio, a pilot says «Alpha, Bravo, Charlie». What is this an example of? | A list of animals | A map of the sea | *A phonetic alphabet, code words for letters | A cooking recipe
test: Why do dictionaries use phonetic symbols? | To show which words are rude | To make the page look colourful | *Both show pronunciation and help learners say words correctly | To show how a word is pronounced
test: «Write it phonetically: "nite" for night.» What is "nite" in this case? | *A phonetic spelling that shows how night sounds | A word that rhymes with kite | A mistake that cannot be used | A type of radio code
exam: Mum says, «Write it phonetically, Sam: "kat" for cat.» What does phonetically mean here? | *In a way that shows how the word sounds | Very loudly | Using a different language | In a way that hides the sound
